  "reflection": "Most mappings in this group were already correct and only required validation. A few minor corrections were made for precise OMOP terminology. For `C-peptide` (rows 1827-1829), the term was changed to the correct OMOP spelling `C peptide`. For a leukocyte count (row 1811), the system `White Blood Cells` was corrected to the lowercase `White blood cells`. In one case of a nucleic acid test (row 1798), `Chlamydia pneumoniae` was updated to the taxonomically newer `Chlamydophila pneumoniae` as suggested by the candidate list and used in LOINC for the analyte itself (as opposed to antibody tests). The candidate generation process failed for the common components `Follicle stimulating hormone` and `Luteinizing hormone`, providing no suggestions. I retained the existing values as they are the correct OMOP terms, but this gap in the candidate list is a significant weakness."
}
